**/__pycache__/

# Buildings are not part of the project: each is its own inputs, its own recipe
# and its own results, and they come and go. What is shared here is the
# generator, and somebody who takes it should get the generator and not a
# stranger's buildings. The skeleton they start from is part of it, so it is the
# one thing under here that is versioned.
#
# `buildings/*` rather than `buildings/`, because git does not look inside an
# ignored directory and the exception below would never be reached.
#
# What keeps the ignored buildings in step with the library is not git, and it
# was a mistake to reach for git for it. It is `tools/lint_buildings.py`, which
# reads every building's calls against the library it actually has and is run by
# `pipeline_selftest` -- so a rename that breaks six untracked buildings turns
# the selftest red the same minute. See the note at the top of that file.
buildings/*
!buildings/__init__.py
!buildings/_template/

tmp/
.claude/settings.json
